# Records a take in demo mode, reviews it and publishes it, and asserts what is on the page by test id. One `step` per line, as in fixtures/tours/files-open.steps:
# `expect <id>` means the tree has a view with that testId; `absent <id>` means it has none. Run in demo mode (AUTORADIO_DEMO=1); the demo build records a
# quiet tone as long as the button was held, reads a fixed sentence as its transcript, and answers the takes routes from fixtures/demo/takes-*.json.
# The app opens on the Autoradio page, so no navigation step. What only a device can prove: the real microphone and AVAudioRecorder file, the on-device recogniser reading it, the radio pausing and resuming around the take
# (console: AUTORADIO take recording started ..., take recorded seconds=<n> bytes=<n> chars=<n>, take published id=<id>), and the Settings prompts.
clock +800 real
tree
expect radio-takes
expect takes-record
shot takes-idle
tap takes-record
clock +4500 real
tree
expect takes-stop
expect takes-elapsed
absent takes-record
shot takes-recording
tap takes-stop
clock +2500 real
tree
expect takes-review
expect takes-transcript
expect takes-publish-line
expect takes-preview
expect takes-rerecord
expect takes-discard
expect takes-publish
shot takes-review
# re-record then discard: nothing was published
tap takes-rerecord
clock +4500 real
tap takes-stop
clock +2500 real
tap takes-discard
clock +600 real
tree
expect takes-record
absent takes-review
# record again and publish
tap takes-record
clock +4500 real
tap takes-stop
clock +2500 real
tap takes-publish
clock +2500 real
clock data
tree
expect takes-published
expect takes-mine-0
expect takes-record
shot takes-published
# delete it
tap takes-delete-0
clock +1500 real
tree
absent takes-mine-0
shot takes-deleted
